


Instruction Set Architecture "isa.h"

            The operation_from_opcode function returns an
            { operation } (a function pointer) corresponding
            to the opcode specified by #0. All inputs result
            in a valid return (possibly a pointer to a
            "no operation" instruction).

            The mnemonic_from_opcode function writes the
            mnemonic (a short string) into the array
            specified by #0 corresponding to the opcode
            specified by #1.

            The opcode_from_mnemonic function returns the
            opcode corresponding to the mnemonic (a short
            string) specified by #0.
